# Settings that are the same for every build of this app, and safe to read.
#
# The two VITE_SUPABASE_* values are deliberately NOT here — they point a build
# at a particular database, so they belong to whoever is deploying rather than
# to the repository. See .env.example.

# The public half of the VAPID pair, for push notifications.
#
# Committed on purpose. It ships inside the JavaScript bundle whatever we do —
# the browser has to hand it to the push service when it subscribes — so there
# is nothing to protect, and keeping it here means any build has it without a
# dashboard setting somebody has to remember. All it does is let a push service
# check who signed a message.
#
# The private half is a secret and lives only in the Edge Function's settings.
# Regenerate the pair with `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`; changing it
# invalidates every existing subscription, so everybody has to turn
# notifications on again.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BBNWZtZClTTANnxm_Rm8osve2dB6kGotyKlyshXkg5Vfqbsed5-_Xn5SI479ScVy350eXREXRlzobMxGkdmnTOE
